---
import BaseLayout from '~/layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Terms of use"
  description="Rules and expectations for using Mindful: reading, intellectual property, limitations, and links to our disclaimer and privacy pages."
>
  <article class="mx-auto max-w-3xl">
    <header class="mb-10">
      <p class="text-xs tracking-[0.3em] text-[var(--muted)] uppercase">Terms of use</p>
      <h1
        class="mt-4 text-5xl leading-tight tracking-tight text-balance sm:text-6xl"
        style="font-family: var(--font-display); font-weight: 500; font-variation-settings: 'opsz' 96;"
      >
        Using Mindful on fair terms.
      </h1>
    </header>

    <div class="prose">
      <p>
        By reading or sharing links to Mindful, you agree to these terms. If something here does
        not work for you, please stop using the site.
      </p>

      <h2>What Mindful is</h2>
      <p>
        Mindful publishes short essays on everyday mental wellbeing. The site is informational
        reading, not a service agreement for therapy, coaching, or crisis support. Our
        <a href="/disclaimer">Disclaimer</a> says more about limits of the content; it is part of
        how we expect the site to be used.
      </p>

      <h2>Not professional care</h2>
      <p>
        Nothing on Mindful replaces advice from a qualified professional. If you rely on any essay
        in place of care, you do so against our intent. Read the disclaimer for crisis guidance.
      </p>

      <h2>Intellectual property</h2>
      <p>
        Text, layout, branding, and original graphics on Mindful belong to us or our licensors
        unless otherwise noted. You may read in a browser, bookmark, and link to pages in a normal,
        non-misleading way. Please do not copy full essays for republication, scrape the site for
        training or bulk reuse, or remove credits without permission. If you would like to reuse
        material, reach out through channels we provide when we have them.
      </p>

      <h2>Third-party services</h2>
      <p>
        Delivery of the site (for example hosting, DNS, and placeholder images) involves
        third-party providers. Their terms and privacy practices apply to what they do on their
        side. We describe our angle on that in <a href="/privacy">Privacy</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>Acceptable use</h2>
      <p>
        Do not try to break, overload, or probe the site in ways that could harm other readers or
        our infrastructure. Do not use Mindful to harass anyone or to automate abusive traffic.
      </p>

      <h2>Links out</h2>
      <p>
        Essays may link elsewhere. We do not control external sites and are not responsible for
        their content, availability, or policies.
      </p>

      <h2>Changes and availability</h2>
      <p>
        We may edit essays, routes, or these terms from time to time. The site may occasionally be
        unavailable for maintenance or reasons outside our control. We do not promise uninterrupted
        access.
      </p>

      <h2>Limitation of liability</h2>
      <p>
        To the fullest extent allowed by law, Mindful and its editors are not liable for indirect,
        incidental, or consequential damages arising from your use of the site or reliance on any
        essay. Our total liability for any claim related to the site should not exceed what you
        paid to use Mindful &mdash; which is zero, because the reading is free.
      </p>

      <h2>Privacy</h2>
      <p>
        For how technical data may be processed when you visit, see <a href="/privacy">Privacy</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
